---
title: "Engineering Economics"
code: "EGR-206"
category: "engineering"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Presents economic analysis of engineering alternatives. Studies economic and cost concepts, calculation of economic equivalence, comparison of alternatives, replacement economy, economic optimization in design and operation, depreciation, and after-tax analysis. Lecture 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
